{% from 'networkpolicy.yml.j2' import networkpolicy with context %}
---
# The subject of this policy is FLARESOLVERR, not prowlarr — it lives in the prowlarr role
# because flaresolverr has no role of its own, and prowlarr is its only caller. prowlarr's own
# policy is the sibling `networkpolicy-prowlarr.yaml.j2`.
#
# It keeps a headless browser that renders attacker-supplied Cloudflare pages reachable by
# prowlarr and nothing else. Without it every workload in
# {{ k8s_namespace }} could reach it — including qbittorrent's untrusted payloads and jellyfin —
# the same argument n8n-broker's policy makes.
#
# INGRESS: the exposure is who reaches this port. The prowlarr-verify Job (templates/verify/job.yaml.j2) checks it on every revision that edits
# this policy or flaresolverr's Deployment, rather than trusting the asymmetry.
#
# Rendered from the shared macro with literal arguments rather than a `netpol_fences` item on
# prowlarr's entry: the port is `prowlarr_k8s_flaresolverr_port`, a role default the inventory
# cannot read, and copying it there as a literal would give the port two sources.
{{ networkpolicy('flaresolverr', prowlarr_k8s_flaresolverr_port, ['prowlarr']) }}
